---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy Policy · Mob" description="Mob collects no personal data. The apps connect only to your own mobd.">
  <article class="doc container-x max-w-3xl pt-20">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-zinc-500">Updated October 23, 2026</p>
    <p>Mob is made of mobd, which runs on your office computer, and the Mob apps for macOS, iPhone, iPad and Android. It runs on your own computers and devices. We operate no server that receives your data.</p>
    <h2>We collect no data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Mob contains no analytics, crash reporting or advertising SDKs, and does not track you.</li>
      <li>The apps connect only to the mobd addresses you add. Conversations, screenshots, files and the live view travel directly between your devices and your office computer.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Data on your devices</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Pairing credentials are kept in the system Keychain (Apple) or Keystore (Android).</li>
      <li>Added computers, settings and a cache of recent conversations are stored in the app and removed when you uninstall it.</li>
      <li>mobd keeps its settings and conversations on your office computer (<code>~/.mobd</code> and <code>~/Library/Application Support/mob</code> on macOS). You manage and delete them.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The agents you run in mobd, such as Codex or Claude Code, send task content to their model providers under your agreement with those providers. Network services such as Tailscale apply their own privacy policies.</p>
    <h2>App permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Camera:</strong> only to scan the pairing QR code. No images are stored.</li>
      <li><strong>Local network:</strong> to reach mobd on your LAN.</li>
      <li><strong>Notifications:</strong> to tell you when the agent needs an answer or a task finishes.</li>
      <li><strong>Microphone:</strong> Mob does not record audio. The description comes from the WebRTC component used for the live view.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>This website uses no cookies, analytics or third-party scripts. Downloads are served from our download server, which may keep standard access logs.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:mob@taoist.dev">mob@taoist.dev</a>. When the policy changes, the date above changes too.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
